{"body":{"asks":"A source brings the world of ones and zeros into the field, but what was once called an integration goes both ways: the field may emanate outward, as a REST endpoint from a structure it defines, a file of TypeScript types, a git repository virtualised from its commits. Is the source then two-way, and what is the interface, which integrates to the engine, beside it?","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M7GJ08SSZN6051"}],"stands":"open"},"id":"1M7GJ0B2MPWP000","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Sources both ways","prev":null}
